meta {
  name: List Recent Triage Records
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{CRM_URL}}/rpa_integrationinboundqueues?$select=rpa_integrationinboundqueueid,rpa_name,rpa_errordetails,rpa_processingresult,rpa_processingentity,rpa_processingstage,statuscode,createdon,modifiedon&$orderby=createdon desc&$top={{top}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  $select: rpa_integrationinboundqueueid,rpa_name,rpa_errordetails,rpa_processingresult,rpa_processingentity,rpa_processingstage,statuscode,createdon,modifiedon
  $orderby: createdon desc
  $top: {{top}}
}

headers {
  Prefer: odata.include-annotations="OData.Community.Display.V1.FormattedValue"
}

vars:pre-request {
  top: 10
}

script:post-response {
  const rows = res.getBody().value ?? [];
  const summary = rows.map(r => {
    let details = {};
    try { details = JSON.parse(r.rpa_errordetails ?? '{}'); } catch { details = { raw: r.rpa_errordetails }; }
    return {
      createdon: r.createdon,
      id: r.rpa_integrationinboundqueueid,
      name: r.rpa_name,
      result: r['rpa_processingresult@OData.Community.Display.V1.FormattedValue'],
      entity: r['rpa_processingentity@OData.Community.Display.V1.FormattedValue'],
      correlationId: details.correlationId,
      fileId: details.fileId,
      caseType: details.caseType,
      failureReason: details.failureReason,
      errorMessage: details.errorMessage
    };
  });
  console.log(summary);
  if (summary.length) {
    bru.setEnvVar("correlationId", summary[0].correlationId);
    bru.setEnvVar("triageRecordId", summary[0].id);
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  The newest triage records the doc-upload integration has written, newest
  first. This is the request to run after forcing a failure: it is how you
  confirm a record was raised at all, and it is the only place the identity
  of the failed submission is recorded.
  
  The entity has no attribute for the CRN, the SBI, the case type or the
  correlation identifier, so fcp-sfd-crm packs all of them into
  rpa_errordetails as JSON:
  
    { "correlationId", "fileId", "caseType", "failureReason", "errorMessage" }
  
  The post-response script parses that JSON for every row and prints a flat
  summary to the Bruno console, then sets {{correlationId}} and
  {{triageRecordId}} from the newest row. Those two env vars are what the
  rest of this folder and the CDP log search key off, so run this first and
  read the correlation id out of the record rather than trying to find it
  before the record exists.
  
  failureReason is one of four values, and is the only thing that
  distinguishes the four conditions from one another. rpa_processingresult
  is Failed for all of them:
  
    contact_not_found_for_crn
    account_not_found_for_sbi
    document_type_not_found
    document_type_metadata_incomplete
  
  The Prefer header adds FormattedValue annotations, so the picklists come
  back as "Failed" and "Doc Upload" alongside their integers rather than as
  bare option-set values.
  
  Note what is *not* populated. fcp-sfd-crm writes exactly four attributes —
  rpa_name, rpa_errordetails, rpa_processingresult and rpa_processingentity.
  rpa_processingstage, statuscode, rpa_xmlmessage, rpa_attempt and
  rpa_dateprocessed are all left empty. They are selected here so that stays
  visible: if a CRM triage view filters on any of them, these records will
  not appear in it.
  
  Raise {{top}} if several runs are being inspected at once.
}
